M2.2: PIC remap + PIT tick (first returning interrupts)

- irq.c: 8259A owned and remapped to vectors 32..47 (ICW1..4, base
  chosen by us); all lines masked pending irq_enable(); handler
  registry + EOI policy (master always, slave for lines 8+); spurious
  counters for IRQ7/15 ghosts.
- pit.c: channel 0, mode 2, divisor 11932 => ~100 Hz; ticks counter.
- isr.s split: trap_common stays dump-and-park (exceptions have no
  return), new irq_common saves/restores 15 GPRs, drops vec+err slots,
  iretq - the FIRST interrupts that return. IRQ stubs keep the same
  17-slot frame so trapframes stay one shape.
- main.c: sti after bring-up; hlt-wait for 300 ticks.

Two bugs caught by the dump itself (the point of M2.1):
1. IDT filled only vectors 0..31 -> first IRQ hit a zero descriptor,
   #GP err=0x202 (external + bad selector) chaser of the truth.
2. Then the fix exposed: trap_ist[32] read out of bounds for v=32..47
   as an IST index -> garbage RSP switch inside the TSS, CR2=-8.
   Now: ist=0 for v>=32, IDT covers 48 entries.

Evidence: "done: ticks=0x12c" = exactly 300 in the 3 s window.
